\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces A perfect probe is not a conserved quantity. Colour is the constraint; marker is the model seed (all three shown, never averaged). \textbf  {Left:} the supervised probe reads true energy almost perfectly. \textbf  {Centre:} the model's own transition preserves it an order of magnitude worse than the label-free scalar. \textbf  {Right:} acting on it fails to reduce rollout energy drift, while the label-free scalar cuts drift on every seed. Probe quality and dynamical relevance rank the three constraints differently.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:probe_vs_operator}{{1}{5}{A perfect probe is not a conserved quantity. Colour is the constraint; marker is the model seed (all three shown, never averaged). \textbf {Left:} the supervised probe reads true energy almost perfectly. \textbf {Centre:} the model's own transition preserves it an order of magnitude worse than the label-free scalar. \textbf {Right:} acting on it fails to reduce rollout energy drift, while the label-free scalar cuts drift on every seed. Probe quality and dynamical relevance rank the three constraints differently.\relax }{figure.caption.15}{}}
